{"Title":"An Act to establish the Massachusetts National Guard Museum in Salem","BillNumber":"S2996","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"S30","Name":"Senate Committee on Ways and Means","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S30","ResponseDate":"2024-12-17T14:03:25.01"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:20:48.74"},{"Id":"JCV0","Name":"John C. Velis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JCV0","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T11:55:47.57"},{"Id":"SSH1","Name":"Steven S. Howitt","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SSH1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T11:55:47.57"},{"Id":"N_C0","Name":"Nick Collins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_C0","ResponseDate":"2023-11-01T13:34:34.7266667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2996/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"Senate, December 19, 2024 -- The committee on Senate Ways and Means, to whom was referred the Senate Bill establish the Massachusetts National Guard Museum in Salem (Senate, No. 2335),- reports, recommending that the same ought to pass with an amendment substituting a new draft (Senate, No. 2996).","DocumentText":"\tChapter 33 of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding the following section:- \r\n\tSection 140.  There shall be a Massachusetts National Guard museum in the city of Salem, the birthplace of the national guard pursuant to section 60 of chapter 2; provided, that said museum shall be the official military museum for the commonwealth.   \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}